1. Preamble and Foundational Vision

The terrestrial biosphere is not an engineered system; it is an inheritance. On the Moon, Mars, or in free‑space habitats, no such inheritance exists. Every breath, every litre of water, every calorie of food, and every gram of recycled waste must be deliberately designed. This programme does not merely train architects of closed life‑support. It trains the theoretical founders of a new science: the discovery of the mathematical, informational, and evolutionary laws that govern the persistence of living civilisations beyond Earth.

The central animating question of the discipline is the Grand Unified Question:

What are the necessary and sufficient conditions for the indefinite persistence of organized life beyond Earth?

From this question, all programme content derives. The answer will be written in thermodynamics, information theory, cybernetics, evolutionary dynamics, computation, and civilisational theory. The graduate is prepared not only to build biospheres, but to generate the fundamental theory that enables multiplanetary humanity.

