Appendix H: Simulation Validation and Digital Twin Consistency

All theoretical results are validated in a high‑fidelity Digital Twin. The twin solves a large system of differential‑algebraic equations and agent‑based social models. Validation protocols include:

· Historical replay: The twin must reproduce the dynamics of Biosphere 2 and other analogue experiments within predefined error bounds.
· Stress‑test scenarios: A standard battery of failure modes (pump failure, crop blight, solar flare, social unrest) is simulated; the control system’s response must match ISS predictions.
· Verification of indices: \Psi_c, \Psi_s, \Psi_e, \Psi_{cv} are numerically computed from twin state data and compared against theoretical thresholds.
· Sensitivity analysis: The influence of unknown parameters on stability indices is quantified via Sobol’ indices, ensuring the design is robust to biological uncertainties.

Only after passing all digital twin acceptance tests is a biosphere architecture deemed ready for physical prototyping.

